{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives","id":997949,"title":"Good, Evil, and Perspectives","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T16:27:51-07:00","id":997949,"title":"Good, Evil, and Perspectives","content":"Has anyone noticed werewolf doesn't give a lot of perspectives beyond the Garou/Fera gaian perspective? For instance we don't really get to see things how a weaver follower would see the world at large.<br /> <br /> Couldn't a BSD see the balance wyrm as a more purifying force, while looking at the wyld as a force of unrestrained, evil corruption and gaia as a neutral/uncaring mother that wishes for her own survival and nothing more.<br /> <br /> While they wouldn't necessarily be correct, it would mix things up to have things going on in the background that the garou are ignorant of and maybe make things more grey vs grey rather than grey vs pitch black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:12:55-07:00","id":997967,"title":"","content":"Well, BSD have walked the Black Spiral, so they are by definition supporters of the Wyrm of Corruption. Of course, they are also quite insane, so they could believe anything. We see the viewpoints of the Weaver followers with the Ananasi, and they think that the Weaver is insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:10:33-07:00","id":997991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=997967#post997967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, BSD have walked the Black Spiral, so they are by definition supporters of the Wyrm of Corruption. Of course, they are also quite insane, so they could believe anything. We see the viewpoints of the Weaver followers with the Ananasi, and they think that the Weaver is insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ananasi believe anything thing their queen ananasa tells them, and said queen wishes to usurp the weaver as she feels she has a better vision for the world. Not something I'd trust.<br /> <br /> Also I do understand that the cannon is wyrm bad, weaver bad, wyld okay sometimes and gaia absolutely good. I just feel that much like how other splats have books from the perspective of the &quot;bad guys&quot;(like guide to the technocracy, or the vampire sabbat books), the established &quot;good guys&quot; don't have all the facts and some of the &quot;bad guys&quot; may not be.<br /> <br /> I feel it would make things more interesting if the wyrm weren't the center of all evil/insanity, but in fact more a neutral uncaring force bent on doing its job as a celestine. It's better for the characters as well if it turns out there's no absolute &quot;right&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; and they have to come to their own conclusions instead, be they to follow garou society or walk alone as a heretic to their peers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:16:05-07:00","id":997992,"title":"","content":"Some BSDs might talk a lot about the Weaver's role in imprisoning the Wyrm and making the world worse, and pontificate about how the world needs the Wyrm to be free. The thing is, they do this, and then do horrible atrocities for their own twisted amusement and self-gratification. Enlightenment does not drive them, or factor into their actions in any way; it's 100% being a total asshole. As for the Weave's point of view, it's probably pretty well covered by the principles espoused by the OneSong and conversion of drones.<br /> <br /> The parts which Garou are ignorant about are in deeply-detailed specifics, like the Opal Prison not actually housing what they think it does or the Nagah being dead, or at the very least, not Gaia's punishment crew, and in the workings of other games' settings. The latter don't really matter, though, because absent reliance on some deep details that are kept from them, the Garou and Fera are entirely correct about the importance of their existence and roles in the cosmos. The grey vs. grey is in how they interact with each other, not their enemies, as different tribes and changers have different ideas about what constitutes objectionable action, beyond the shit that BSDs do. Ratkin, for example, exist to bring humanity down to more reasonable numbers, and they do so by every means but direct action (or at least used to), such as diseases, stealing food, or sabotage of key industries that would hurt the most. Garou find such methods to be highly distasteful and cruel, on account of how their culture is an honor-driven warrior culture, but they have no real sanction for this, and their massacres of the wererats in ages past are well known for being a mistake..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T19:38:18-07:00","id":998023,"title":"","content":"I agree, cWoD is largely grey versus black (when it is not black versus black), as morally complicated characters often find themselves facing truly evil enemies. <br /> <br /> While grey versus grey exists, it is more tragedy than anything else, like the conflict between the Camarilla and the Garou Nation. While neither group is white, they could be useful to each other, but it largely the blindness caused by their own sense of their own importance that drives their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:07:04-07:00","id":998034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998023#post998023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, cWoD is largely grey versus black (when it is not black versus black), as morally complicated characters often find themselves facing truly evil enemies.<br /> <br /> While grey versus grey exists, it is more tragedy than anything else, like the conflict between the Camarilla and the Garou Nation. While neither group is white, they could be useful to each other, but it largely the blindness caused by their own sense of their own importance that drives their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the camarilla is so much &quot;grey&quot; as a less dark shade of black to the sabbat. They are an order of immortal blood suckers that treats the lives of fellow kindred and humans as pawns/playthings/the occasional light snack after all. There really isn't enough &quot;white morality&quot; in place even cancel all the harm they and the sabbat do, the world would honestly be better without them. Good is temporary and you're immortal, such is the struggle of vampire.<br /> <br /> I don't think grey vs. black morality is very good for any stories outside of tragedies. &quot;Sure the garou have royally failed and they constantly war with themselves, but they're not That bad. I mean look at the alternative(points at nearest wyrm spawn)&quot; is the excuse that it ultimately comes down to. Players end up unable to do anything meaningful, stories tend to become repetitive angst sessions, and werewolves are one again forced to play along a system of beliefs that were decided of beliefs decided long before they were born regardless of what they think.<br /> <br /> I just feel it takes something away when a player can't decide that they don't like the traditions of the garou without being labled as wyrmspawn or a BSD potential. In a whits vs black world you can at least believe in what you're doing, and in a grey vs. grey there's even a chance for some middle ground to be found. Not in grey vs black though, the grey side has no reason to change and thus stays corrupt while all the alternatives are too horrible to count as a real choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:34:24-07:00","id":998050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998034#post998034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the camarilla is so much &quot;grey&quot; as a less dark shade of black to the sabbat. They are an order of immortal blood suckers that treats the lives of fellow kindred and humans as pawns/playthings/the occasional light snack after all. There really isn't enough &quot;white morality&quot; in place even cancel all the harm they and the sabbat do, the world would honestly be better without them. Good is temporary and you're immortal, such is the struggle of vampire.<br /> <br /> I don't think grey vs. black morality is very good for any stories outside of tragedies. &quot;Sure the garou have royally failed and they constantly war with themselves, but they're not That bad. I mean look at the alternative(points at nearest wyrm spawn)&quot; is the excuse that it ultimately comes down to. Players end up unable to do anything meaningful, stories tend to become repetitive angst sessions, and werewolves are one again forced to play along a system of beliefs that were decided of beliefs decided long before they were born regardless of what they think.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could play it that way, but as the intro comics for W20 and W20 Changing Breeds show, the pendulum is swinging the other way. You just have to figure out where to push it, and how hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just feel it takes something away when a player can't decide that they don't like the traditions of the garou without being labled as wyrmspawn or a BSD potential. </div> </div> </div>That takes a lot more than just a simple question, especially if you're a Ragabash, because that's their job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a whits vs black world you can at least believe in what you're doing, and in a grey vs. grey there's even a chance for some middle ground to be found. Not in grey vs black though, the grey side has no reason to change and thus stays corrupt while all the alternatives are too horrible to count as a real choice. </div> </div> </div>As I said, the grey vs. grey is in coming to head in quite likely a non-violent manner with the methods of other Garou and in reconciling with the Fera. The entire Amazon War plot arc revolved around this, as the werewolves were forced to come to terms with the ways that they weren't helping in the struggle (such as how they tried to take charge all the time, and drafted spirits into being the empowering force for many newly-created war fetishes) and eventually leaving at the behest of the Balam and Mokole.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T21:16:47-07:00","id":998071,"title":"","content":"Garou can believe in what they are doing and in fact everything they see, hear, learn, touch and smell reinforce those beliefs at least in cosmology.<br /> <br /> Using my favorite example a school bus full of children break down outside the bawn of a Child of Gaia caern the Children of Gaia instantly spring into action directing kinfolk to help or at least arrange for a tow truck. The bus is removed and 5 years later the private school spawning ground for formori alum return and massacre the Sept with their allies the BSD pack Tricks the Foolish.<br /> The same scenario, but the Garou use Sense Wyrm and discover a horror in the making. Do they slaughter the still human children, do they perform a Rite of Cleansing, do they do nothing, does the Sept send a pack to investigate? All of these questions aren't easily answered unless you're playing a murder hobo they have a real impact on a story and in fact an entire Chronicle could easily be written around this scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T22:06:50-07:00","id":998089,"title":"","content":"I would think that they trace the source of the contamination to its source and then arrange to cleanse the children. It would not be a bad idea for a chronicle, though the children would not show up on Sense Wyrm unless they were already fomori or Possessed a Humanity 3-. A more manageable scenario would be having Wyrm contaminated packed lunches on the bus and having that lead to a plot to transform a significant proportion of the children into fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:08:08-07:00","id":998121,"title":"","content":"My theory. <br /> <br /> The Gaian spirits are the problem. They've created broods and hierachys and are invested in the current world and their continued existence. <br /> Joining a tribe gives yourself to the eternal service of a spirit (rather like an infernalist) The reason why garou are taught to despise ronin is because ronin are outside the power of these powerful spirits.They haven't unknowingly bargained their souls away, and are thus a threat/in the wrong for not being property of a tribal spirit. Originally, all garou were ronin, but some traded their allegiance for power. Ronin are the best garou, in a similar way to how caitiff are the purest of vampires. Everyone despises the pure ones, and they don't have the organisation to fight back. <br /> <br /> The spirits are entirely selfish creatures. <br /> <br /> The garou fight the wyrm because their totems tell them to (Gaia told the totems to tell them for her, allegedly) Really, the Totems fight the wyrm because, well, the wyrm spirits threaten them personally. The dear fears death, the wolf fears hunger, the rabbit fears disease. Every totem has a vested interest in keeping the wheel of ages where it is, to keep them alive for as long as possible, because some day (as cockroach, crocodile, shark and dragonfly tell it) Those that don't survive will be replaced by the next generation of spirits, and the survivors will loose substantial power anyway.<br /> <br /> Gaia is a trick. You're all fools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T01:45:23-07:00","id":998141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998089#post998089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that they trace the source of the contamination to its source and then arrange to cleanse the children. It would not be a bad idea for a chronicle, though the children would not show up on Sense Wyrm unless they were already fomori or Possessed a Humanity 3-. A more manageable scenario would be having Wyrm contaminated packed lunches on the bus and having that lead to a plot to transform a significant proportion of the children into fomori.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or the bus is actually the Wyrm Tainted incubator. Which has a bane bound to the engine that causes it to break down when it Senses Gaia..If I scripted this out for a chronicle I would look at several different options. I won't be using this anytime soon my players are used to &quot;Children of the Corn&quot; scenarios, and live in fear any time the word Derry is mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T02:21:26-07:00","id":998151,"title":"","content":"There are no absolutes. Good and Evil are illusionary concepts. What is good for some is bad for others, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nobody who takes their commitments seriously considers themselves to be a bad person. Everything they do, from their perspective, is morally justified.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Gaia may be good and the Wyrm may be bad... but that's the story as told by Werewolves... <i>who are servants of Gaia and enemies of the Wyrm.</i><br /> <br /> I imagine the servants of the Wyrm might have something quite different to say about their master, and wholly different views about Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:44:23-07:00","id":998223,"title":"","content":"Well, I do think that the corruption and madness of the Wyrm is fairly well documented by multiple sources (Werewolves and Mages). Considering that the majority of the servants are pedophiles, rapists, and serial killers, I think that the minions of the Wyrm are evil. While mentally healthy people are incapable of seriously considering themselves to be evil, psychopaths and sociopaths do not care and only desire to gain pleasure and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:52:16-07:00","id":998350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998223#post998223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I do think that the corruption and madness of the Wyrm is fairly well documented by multiple sources (Werewolves and Mages). Considering that the majority of the servants are pedophiles, rapists, and serial killers, I think that the minions of the Wyrm are evil. While mentally healthy people are incapable of seriously considering themselves to be evil, psychopaths and sociopaths do not care and only desire to gain pleasure and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or there could be other things at work. The book possessed mentions that some of the possessed can change how their taint is read by others, so just as many of those &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; may be gorgons or drones leading the garou on a wild goose chase.<br /> <br /> Corruption&quot; always seemed like it'd be a wyld thing to me, as corruption isn't necessarily destructive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:29:01-07:00","id":998540,"title":"","content":"Corruption is different than disease and decay though. Disease and decay are biological or physical processes while Corruption is a mental or spiritual process. By definition, Corruption is unnatural while disease and decay are natural.<br /> <br /> For example, death is a natural process and, in order for new life the flourish, old life must die. If accidents or violence do not cause death, then disease and decay will likely cause death (parasites and toxins usually weaken an individual and are rarely direct causes of death in nature). The Wyld, by creating new life in the form of diseases and parasites, promotes the natural cycle. The Wyld also creates fungi, which use decay to remove corpses, which also promotes the natural cycle.<br /> <br /> However, immortality is a perversion of nature, it is old life refusing to make room for new life, and represents Corruption. Since the Wyld can only create, immortality can only be achieved by appealing to the Weaver (by strengthening the order with the body) or the Wyrm (by redirecting destruction from the body). In this case, the source of Corruption is not the Wyld but, instead, the Weaver or the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:58:18-07:00","id":998596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998540#post998540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corruption is different than disease and decay though. Disease and decay are biological or physical processes while Corruption is a mental or spiritual process. By definition, Corruption is unnatural while disease and decay are natural.<br /> <br /> For example, death is a natural process and, in order for new life the flourish, old life must die. If accidents or violence do not cause death, then disease and decay will likely cause death (parasites and toxins usually weaken an individual and are rarely direct causes of death in nature). The Wyld, by creating new life in the form of diseases and parasites, promotes the natural cycle. The Wyld also creates fungi, which use decay to remove corpses, which also promotes the natural cycle.<br /> <br /> However, immortality is a perversion of nature, it is old life refusing to make room for new life, and represents Corruption. Since the Wyld can only create, immortality can only be achieved by appealing to the Weaver (by strengthening the order with the body) or the Wyrm (by redirecting destruction from the body). In this case, the source of Corruption is not the Wyld but, instead, the Weaver or the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um, disease and fungi are wyrmish as they destroy things(I believe this is also mentioned in the books as the reminders of why the wyrm is still a necessary part of the triat). I don't know if that was a typo or not, but just in case.<br /> <br /> Madness, Deformation, and Physical mutations are normally blamed on the wyrm even though these don't directly destroy anything(because the garou typically blame almost anything bad or &quot;evil&quot; on the wyrm). I feel these should be attributed the wyld, as the harmful mutations caused by random creation and chance(which are More common in nature than helpful ones.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:32:07-07:00","id":998609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998596#post998596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Um, disease and fungi are wyrmish as they destroy things(I believe this is also mentioned in the books as the reminders of why the wyrm is still a necessary part of the triat). I don't know if that was a typo or not, but just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't Wyrm-enough, even Balance Wyrm-enough, to register, though. They're just organisms trying to survive..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Madness, Deformation, and Physical mutations are normally blamed on the wyrm even though these don't directly destroy anything(because the garou typically blame almost anything bad or &quot;evil&quot; on the wyrm). I feel these should be attributed the wyld, as the harmful mutations caused by random creation and chance(which are More common in nature than helpful ones.) </div> </div> </div>Per the powers shared by both Gorgons and Fomori, they would be both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:05:29-07:00","id":998995,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm is the Wyrm of Corruption. Its minions do not even seem to disagree on that point, they embrace Corruption. They are trying to tear down the world and remake it in a more pleasing form for them.<br /> <br /> Madness, Deformation, and Negative Mutations are created by damage to the organism, which is a form of Corruption (positive mutations occur when the damage changes a gene into something useful, which would be a form of Creation). Madness is caused by the Corruption of the brain, Deformation by the Corruption of the body, and Negative Mutations by the Corruption of the DNA. The Wyld really has nothing to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 11-05-2016, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:21:07-07:00","id":998999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998995#post998995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm is the Wyrm of Corruption. Its minions do not even seem to disagree on that point, they embrace Corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>This mostly.<br /> <br /> While you don't really get a sense of the world from the Weaver's perspective (though Drones are a good indicator), they do actually give you the Wyrm's (or at least it's servants) in the various Books of the Wyrm/BSD sections. The Wyrm isn't supposed to be a sympathetic villain. It isn't the Technocracy equivalent of Mage. I suppose I don't necessarily understand the goal of trying to un-villain the Wyrm's minions.<br /> I guess DNA is the closest you get. Their motivations are generally for the greater good. And yet they are still clearly antagonists for most games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:26:33-07:00","id":999000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=998999#post998999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This mostly.<br /> <br /> While you don't really get a sense of the world from the Weaver's perspective (though Drones are a good indicator), they do actually give you the Wyrm's (or at least it's servants) in the various Books of the Wyrm/BSD sections. The Wyrm isn't supposed to be a sympathetic villain. It isn't the Technocracy equivalent of Mage. I suppose I don't necessarily understand the goal of trying to un-villain the Wyrm's minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cosmic wars in fiction can get tiring after a while, I suppose. Still, there's a vast amount of other things to make sympathetic. The Triat (all three of them) shouldn't be among them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess DNA is the closest you get. Their motivations are generally for the greater good. And yet they are still clearly antagonists for most games. </div> </div> </div>Well, they go far over the edge with that whole &quot;make a virus to wipe out everyone with this sequence, and damn the collateral damage!&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:33:29-07:00","id":999002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999000#post999000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cosmic wars in fiction can get tiring after a while, I suppose. Still, there's a vast amount of other things to make sympathetic. The Triat (all three of them) shouldn't be among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, entirely possible I don't get the underlying point. The Gray on Gray portions of Werewolf in my experience come from Garou/Garou and Garou/Fera interactions. All parties can mean well and everything still go to hell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:08:13-07:00","id":999021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999002#post999002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, entirely possible I don't get the underlying point. The Gray on Gray portions of Werewolf in my experience come from Garou/Garou and Garou/Fera interactions. All parties can mean well and everything still go to hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I just disagree with making all or most of the evil in the world come from one point(I.E. the wyrm). The Grey on Grey that comes from the fera fighting amongst themselves seems a little stupid to me as they all agree they're Supposed to work together for the sake of Gaia, but don't. They end up destroying themselves and whatever goals they set over stupid pride or petty greed, and I can only feel they deserve whatever they put themselves through.<br /> <br /> The wyrm on the other hand is blamed for everything evil/wrong/unpleasant in the world, yet it is repeatedly stated that it's somehow still a necessary force. It's like the christian devil, it feels like a scapegoat for the people to blame all their problems on so they don't have to come to terms with the fact that they and those around them are responsible for their lives(I'm also christian so please don't make this a religious arguement)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:27:02-07:00","id":999056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999021#post999021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess I just disagree with making all or most of the evil in the world come from one point(I.E. the wyrm).</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't though. Humanity at least, does a majority of the damage it does all on its own. That damage just happens to feed the Wyrm (and the Weaver too usually). There are times where &quot;the Wyrm&quot; inspires the damage, but that isn't <i>always</i> the case. It's the World of Darkness. Things are pretty bleak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999021#post999021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Grey on Grey that comes from the fera fighting amongst themselves seems a little stupid to me as they all agree they're Supposed to work together for the sake of Gaia, but don't. They end up destroying themselves and whatever goals they set over stupid pride or petty greed, and I can only feel they deserve whatever they put themselves through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Humans manage to not get along and kill each other just as often. No reason Supernatural creatures full of Rage should magically be better at getting along for the greater good. To their credit, the Fera are realizing it and making headway on getting along again in a few parts of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999021#post999021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The wyrm on the other hand is blamed for everything evil/wrong/unpleasant in the world, yet it is repeatedly stated that it's somehow still a necessary force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on who you ask. The Weaver is blamed for a lot of problems as well (sometimes over the Wyrm). And I would say the Wyld only escapes blame for things generally because it is (arguably) currently the weakest of the Triat. And the Wyrm of Balance is necessary. The Wyrm of Corruption is not. They really are 2 different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:59:36-07:00","id":999065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999056#post999056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't though. Humanity at least, does a majority of the damage it does all on its own. That damage just happens to feed the Wyrm (and the Weaver too usually). There are times where &quot;the Wyrm&quot; inspires the damage, but that isn't <i>always</i> the case. It's the World of Darkness. Things are pretty bleak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it odd went things are labeled &quot;wyrmish&quot; or &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; even if said evil thing has little to do with distruction. For instance, other splats like vampires, demons, etc. can reek of wyrm taint even if they aren't particularly destructive or &quot;evil&quot;. Even a social vampire with low humanity will reek of wyrm taint, and demons All reek of wyrm taint(even reconcilers with torment 1).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999056#post999056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Humans manage to not get along and kill each other just as often. No reason Supernatural creatures full of Rage should magically be better at getting along for the greater good. To their credit, the Fera are realizing it and making headway on getting along again in a few parts of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I also believe said humans deserve what they've brought on themselves and that many of their actions are stupid. I'm not saying that the fera vs fera thing isn't realistic(though that doesn't make it any less dumb), they just don't have a good reason to be enemies in the first place.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999056#post999056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on who you ask. The Weaver is blamed for a lot of problems as well (sometimes over the Wyrm). And I would say the Wyld only escapes blame for things generally because it is (arguably) currently the weakest of the Triat. And the Wyrm of Balance is necessary. The Wyrm of Corruption is not. They really are 2 different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they though? The only sources the garou have on the subject are their own legends, whats left of pacts returning from the field, and the words of ancient spirits who talk so symbolically that it's hard to tell if they're giving you a lesson in thermodynamics or a recipe for roast beef. They know things about as best as they can interpret them.<br /> <br /> For all we know, the chaos and corruption in malpheas could be cause by a literal war between the wyld and wyrm happening there(wyld spirits invading through the fonts there and masquerading as banes to sow chaos and madness across malpheas). While that may not be the case, would the werewolves honestly know if the triat themselves were keeping something from them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T22:24:56-07:00","id":999070,"title":"","content":"Because they can talk to the former servants of the Wyrm of Balance. Heck, some of their Totems are former Incarna of the Wyrm of Balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T22:35:37-07:00","id":999076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999065#post999065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find it odd went things are labeled &quot;wyrmish&quot; or &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; even if said evil thing has little to do with distruction. For instance, other splats like vampires, demons, etc. can reek of wyrm taint even if they aren't particularly destructive or &quot;evil&quot;. Even a social vampire with low humanity will reek of wyrm taint, and demons All reek of wyrm taint(even reconcilers with torment 1).</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampires are corrupt, not destructive. That's why the smell of the Wyrm (because the &quot;current&quot; Wyrm is the embodiment of corruption). For Demons though (and I am admittedly less versed in them, even from a Werewolf perspective), I don't know that they all are &quot;of the Wyrm&quot;. And even that though, could be residual from their time in the Abyss (a different Abyss than Werewolf's, but that's another discussion). Garou aren't automatically enemies of anything that has Wyrm taint. Wyrm taint is supposed to be used as an indicator to learn more. Not to murder on sight.<br /> Either way though, Garou should be for Gaia, which right now from their perspective is being attacked by the Wyrm. If sometime later the Wyrm was put in balance and the Wyld was destroying Gaia, they would then be fighting the Wyld primarily. That though would be a completely different world than the setting as presented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999065#post999065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not saying that the fera vs fera thing isn't realistic(though that doesn't make it any less dumb), they just don't have a good reason to be enemies in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feuds are a hard thing to forget, especially when so many have died. I agree it's dumb, but so are most real life wars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999065#post999065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are they though?</div> </div> </div> </div>In setting, yes they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999065#post999065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only sources the garou have on the subject are their own legends, whats left of pacts returning from the field, and the words of ancient spirits who talk so symbolically that it's hard to tell if they're giving you a lesson in thermodynamics or a recipe for roast beef. They know things about as best as they can interpret them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also their Ancestors that they can actually talk to. And the memories of at least 2 of the Fera (Mokole and Ratkin...and some still living Rokea actually) and several Spirit Realms you can go to to actually live through or see the past. And all of the (Middle) Umbra being set up the way it is between the Supernals. Also, not all Spirits talk in complete riddles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999065#post999065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For all we know, the chaos and corruption in malpheas could be cause by a literal war between the wyld and wyrm happening there (wyld spirits invading through the fonts there and masquerading as banes to sow chaos and madness across malpheas).</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be what's going on in Malfeas I suppose if you as a ST wanted to go that route. There would be evidence though I would think. The Supernals clashing usually isn't a subtle thing. Especially not when Realms are at stake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999065#post999065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While that may not be the case, would the werewolves honestly know if the triat themselves were keeping something from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Triat generally doesn't &quot;keep things to themselves&quot;. That train of thought personifies them too much for my taste. But no, if things were running like that so far above mortal(-ish) perceptions, it would be difficult for the Garou to know any better. But I don't know that that is a convincing argument. If the world fundamentally operates differently then you <i>can</i> know or perceive, you can't be blamed for being on the (possible) wrong side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997949-good-evil-and-perspectives?p=999070#post999070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they can talk to the former servants of the Wyrm of Balance. Heck, some of their Totems are former Incarna of the Wyrm of Balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This too. Hell, depending on how you view it, there are actually Aspects and servants of the Wyrm of Balance still kicking around (the Dragon of Pangea and the Wani).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T23:09:20-07:00","id":999085,"title":"","content":"Now, this does not mean that some minions of the Wyrm cannot be heroically fighting against the Corruption within their souls. For example, any Fomori with Autonomy 7+ is probably sufficiently independent from their Bane that they can decide their own actions and some of them are going to decide to fight against the Wyrm. I have introduced fomori to VtM, so they have Humanity and Virtues, so I cap maximum Humanity at permanent Autonomy. I also have been it that Sense Wyrm can only detect them as fomori if their Humanity drops below '7'.<br /> <br /> I use a group called the Sisterhood of Lilith, which is an underground rail for female fomori who train their members to resist the influence of their Banes. I give them a proprietary Hedge Magic, Corruption Resistance, which retroactively increases their initial Power Points by one per level and retroactively increases their temporary Autonomy by two points per dot of permanent Autonomy sacrificed per level of Corruption Resistance. While they may not buy back permanent Autonomy, the extra Power Points and temporary Autonomy gives them flexibility and allows them to avoid further Corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}